{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-evap-permeation fixture",
    "description": "The `process-evap-permeation` fixture: 128 rows of MOVESOutput computed from the snapshot's own INPUT tables. Ports docs/evap-permeation.md -- the activity chain A1-A10 and the cohort structure C1-C4 of docs/evap-leaks.md, this process's own source-bin key rule C2', the evaporative operating-mode distribution E1-E3, and the calculator's six steps PC-1 ... PC-6.\n\nWHAT IS COMPUTED AND WHAT IS READ, because that is the whole question a fixture has to answer honestly.\n\nCOMPUTED, from the input tables and nothing else: the activity, the cohort fractions, the fuel-usage rebase, the operating-mode distribution including the two zeros PC-2b's soak modes enter at, the source-bin weighted permeation rate, the fuel adjustment, the temperature adjustment, the emission and the SCC. `sho`, `sourcehours`, `sourcebindistributionfuelusage_11_26161_2020`, `opmodedistributiontemp`, `fractionofoperating`, `coldsoaktanktemperature`, `quarterhourtemperature` and `MOVESOutput` are all generator output or expected output and none of them is a `data_sources` entry here. `evp_movesoutput` is declared, as its siblings are, so that the other half of the comparison is version-controlled beside the inputs; it is consumed by nothing.\n\nREAD, and it is ONE table: `averagetanktemperature`, 288 cells. That is TankTemperatureGenerator TTG-5's output, and it is a scope decision docs/evap-permeation.md 8.1 states and measures rather than a value this document could not reach. TTG-5's three operating modes come from TTG-1 (mode 151, the quarter-hour recurrence, which components/tank_temperature.esm computes and checks against 96 QuarterHourTemperature, 96 QuarterHourTankTemperature and 24 ColdSoakTankTemperature rows) and from TTG-4a/TTG-4b (modes 300 and 150), whose walk over SampleVehicleTrip's 37,216 rows is finding F28 plus two variable-cardinality expansions the format has no index set for (F5, F14). Read the whole table rather than half of it, because the half that TTG-1 would supply is inert here: `omd_opModeFraction` for modes 150 and 151 is exactly 0 on both day types, COMPUTED in this document from A10's on-network identity, so the 96 cold-soak cells and the 96 hot-soak cells reach the answer multiplied by zero and only the 96 operating-mode cells are load-bearing. `./run-permeation-oracle.sh` computes mode 151 and reads the other 192; the difference between the two reads is 96 cells that cannot move a single output digit, and `tankTemperatureSoakWeight` asserts that here. docs/esm-conventions.md 23 is the rule this follows and 34.2 is what it adds.\n\nWHAT IS NOT THE LEAKS FIXTURE, and it is not only the calculator. The source bin's DIMENSIONS are per (sourceTypeID, polProcessID): `sourcetypepolprocess.isRegClassReqd` is 'N' for polProcessID 111 where it is 'Y' for 113, so SourceBinDistributionGenerator collapses `regClassID` to 0 in every bin of this snapshot and a cohort carrying the sample vehicle's regulatory class 20 matches nothing at all. `run_isRegClassReqd` reads the flag and `coh_binRegClassID` applies it; `sourceBinRegClassZeroCount` measures that all 80 bins here carry 0. docs/esm-conventions.md 34.1.\n\nTHERE IS NO I/M BLEND. `EvaporativePermeationCalculator`'s 25 INPUT_TABLES contain neither `IMCoverage` nor `IMFactor` and `pollutantprocessassoc` marks polProcessID 111 `isAffectedByEvapIM = 'N'`, so the identity blend the leaks and vapour-venting fixtures carry is absent here rather than zero-weighted. A fixture that inherited it would be modelling a step MOVES does not run.\n\nCOMPUTED, and worth saying so because a reader would assume otherwise: the SHAPES. The activity relation's 82 rows are `n_agecategory x n_runspecday` and the cohort relation's 164 are `n_agecategory x n_runspecsourcefueltype`, both metaparameter expressions over extents the runtime discovers from the files (esm-spec 9.7.6).\n\nDECLARED: one number, `n_outputCohort` = 64, and the block structure of the output relation, for the reasons fixtures/process-evap-leaks.esm gives at length -- materialising the surviving cohorts as an index set is finding F5's value invention and the `ragged` kind is F14. `cohortSurvivorCount` computes 64 from the chain and a test pins the two together.\n\nNO ELEMENT TYPE IS DECLARED, deliberately, for the reason docs/esm-conventions.md 18.4 gives: MOVES stores these working tables in FLOAT and evaluates in MariaDB's DOUBLE, so the reference for this chain IS binary64 arithmetic.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"],
    "tags": ["moves", "onroad", "evaporative", "permeation", "fixture", "process-evap-permeation"]
  },

  "data_sources": {
