            { "variable": "coh_tankTemperatureGroupID", "time": 0.0, "expected": 5.0, "coords": { "cohort_rows": 41 } },
            { "variable": "cohDay_tempAdjustByMode", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.9136768532915025, "coords": { "cohort_rows": 1, "runspecday_rows": 1, "evap_op_mode_rows": 1 } },
            { "variable": "cohDay_tempAdjustByMode", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.6193683118130984, "coords": { "cohort_rows": 1, "runspecday_rows": 1, "evap_op_mode_rows": 2 } },
            { "variable": "cohDay_tempAdjustByMode", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.7585395249127063, "coords": { "cohort_rows": 1, "runspecday_rows": 1, "evap_op_mode_rows": 3 } },
            { "variable": "cohDay_tempAdjustByMode", "time": 0.0, "expected": 1.129609590348527, "coords": { "cohort_rows": 41, "runspecday_rows": 1, "evap_op_mode_rows": 1 } },
            { "variable": "cohDay_weightedTemperatureAdjust", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.7585395249127063, "coords": { "cohort_rows": 1, "runspecday_rows": 1 } },
            { "variable": "cohDay_weightedTemperatureAdjust", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.6743793637126327, "coords": { "cohort_rows": 1, "runspecday_rows": 2 } },
            { "variable": "cohDay_weightedTemperatureAdjust", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.9111967603338292, "coords": { "cohort_rows": 41, "runspecday_rows": 1 } },
            { "variable": "cohDay_weightedTemperatureAdjust", "time": 0.0, "expected": 0.7346185293115818, "coords": { "cohort_rows": 41, "runspecday_rows": 2 } }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "the_worked_examples_reach_movesoutput",
          "description": "PC-5 and PC-6 at ten cells, in both day types. The snapshot stores 0.0870885, 0.102325, 0.353062, 2.90418e-05, 1.45703e-05, 0.294697, 0.346259, 1.0834, 4.93046e-05 and 6.18085e-05 against the values pinned here; the worst difference is 6.174e-06, which is the reference's six-significant-figure column storage of its own intermediates and not accumulated error. What breaks if this is wrong: every factor of the whole chain is in these numbers. ./run-permeation-oracle.sh reaches the same values from the same tables by a different route -- per (pollutant-process, source type, regulatory class, model year, fuel type) key rather than per cohort -- which is what makes a disagreement here attributable to the document rather than to the specification.",
